## Figure legends

**Figure 1.** Kidney share of AlphaGenome human output tracks by assay modality.
Bars show kidney parenchyma tracks as a percentage of all tracks of that
modality, with counts to the right of each bar. Transcription-factor ChIP and
ATAC are highlighted. Kidney parenchyma excludes urinary tract structures and the
HEK293 lineage, both reported separately in the text. The four splice-site
tracks are annotation-derived, carry no biosample and are not shown.

**Figure 2.** Per-tissue Spearman correlation between predicted and observed eQTL
effects, with 95% confidence intervals, for all 49 GTEx tissues. Tissues are
ordered by the number of successfully scored variant-gene pairs, fewest at the
bottom, and that number is given in the right-hand column. Kidney cortex is
highlighted. The dashed vertical line is the unweighted mean across tissues.

**Figure 3.** Width of the 95% confidence interval on Spearman's rho against the
number of successfully scored variant-gene pairs, one point per GTEx tissue, log
scale on the horizontal axis. Kidney cortex is shown as a filled diamond and the
dashed line marks the median interval width across the other tissues. Interval
width is governed by the number of pairs scored; kidney's position reflects its
sample size (section 3.6).

**Figure 4.** Specificity control, using the same 58 scored kidney variant-gene
pairs throughout. (A) Spearman correlation between observed kidney cortex eQTL
effects and predictions taken from each of 54 GTEx tissue outputs in turn, kidney
cortex highlighted. (B) Paired bootstrap difference in rho between each of the
eight highest-ranked comparator outputs and the kidney output, with 95%
confidence intervals, unadjusted for multiplicity. Each of the eight intervals
shown includes zero. Across all 53 comparators none showed a significantly higher
correlation than kidney, while kidney's advantage excluded zero against 10 of
them.
